==Location and Uses==
==={{TFH|-}}===
{{Descriptions TFH}}
Keese Wings are silver-rarity [[Material]]s awarded for completing the following [[Level]]s and [[Drablands Challenge]]s of the [[Volcano]]. The number in parentheses is how many of the three [[Treasure Chest]]s at the end of the Level contain a Keese Wing; each of the [[Links]] may open just one Chest.

*'''[[Hinox Mine]]''', ''"Don't pop any balloons!"'' (1)
*'''[[Den of Flames]]''', ''"Avoid the volcanic rocks!"'' (1)
*'''[[Fire Temple]]''', ''"Clear within the time limit!"'' (1)
*'''Fire Temple''', ''"Only Bombs-no swords!"'' (2)

They can also be won in the [[Coliseum]] and [[Daily Riches]], or purchased from the [[Street Merchant]] for 500 [[Rupee]]s each.

Keese Wings are one of the Materials used to make the [[Energy Gear]] [[Outfit]].<ref name="E 128"/>

==={{BotW|-}}===
In {{BotW}}, Keese Wings are commonly dropped by [[Keese]] when defeated. As is the case with other [[Monster Part]]s, they can be combined with critters in a [[Cooking Pot]] to make all kinds of [[Elixir]]s. They can also be used at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]] to make Gray [[Dye]] or exchanged for [[Mon]] at the [[Fang and Bone]]. There are three variations of Keese Wings: [[Fire Keese Wing]]s, [[Electric Keese Wing]]s, and [[Ice Keese Wing]]s, which come from the relating variation of species.

Three Keese Wings, as well as three [[Rushroom]]s, are needed to upgrade each piece of the [[Climbing Set]] to level ★.
{{Material Armors|BotW|Keese Wing}}

==={{TotK|-}}===
Keese Wings return as [[Item]]s in {{TotK}}.

